{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123393","id":4501193431,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDErC1w","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123393","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123393.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123393.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123393","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123393/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123393/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123393/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/099b075316780710ff4bfaef11ebc803c153ab62","number":123393,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix D3D12 freeze/crash from abrupt Play-session termination on Windows","user":{"login":"JackHeinrich","id":131808024,"node_id":"U_kgDOB9s7GA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131808024?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackHeinrich","html_url":"https://github.com/JackHeinrich","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackHeinrich/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackHeinrich/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackHeinrich/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackHeinrich/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackHeinrich/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackHeinrich/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackHeinrich/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackHeinrich/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JackHeinrich/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes an issue with the D3D12 causing inconsistent freezes when running a project as well as semi-frequently causing graphics device timeouts on AMD GPUs. This issue was caused by the Play/Stop/Reload workflow abruptly `TerminateProcess()`ing game instances that hold a full screen D3D12 swap chain, racing with the driver's asynchronous swap-chain tear down.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThis fix was tested on a device with an AMD RX 6600 XT graphics card running Windows 11. Numerous play / reload cycles were repeated with zero freezes or graphics device timeouts after building Godot with these changes. Also specifically tested multi-instance playing and stopping, stopping while paused at a debugger break point, and verifying that there were no orphaned processes.\r\n\r\nI would like to make reviewers aware that I am not a seasoned C++ developer and the code in this PR is at their discretion to improve upon or rewrite. I hope that if anything, that the reviewers will become aware of what this PR highlights as an issue and that they might use this fix as a foundation for a more refined solution.\r\n\r\n## AI Disclosure\r\n\r\nClaude Code was used substantially to diagnose the root cause of this issue by analyzing crash logs and driver/GPU traces, as well as writing the implementation.\r\n","labels":[{"id":205417413,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyMDU0MTc0MTM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:windows","name":"platform:windows","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platfo